-- Q1169: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [medium/L3]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both scenarios require the same ''more likely than not'' standard because disclosure has no effect on the penalty threshold under Section 6694","The undisclosed position must meet a ''substantial authority'' standard (roughly 40%), while the disclosed position need only meet a ''reasonable basis'' standard (roughly 20%), because disclosure gives the IRS notice to evaluate the position","The disclosed position requires ''substantial authority'' while the undisclosed position requires only ''reasonable basis,'' because hidden positions receive more lenient treatment under the Code","Both scenarios require only a ''realistic possibility of success'' standard (33%) because Section 6694 applies a single uniform threshold to all return positions"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Section 6694(a) establishes a two-tier penalty standard based on disclosure. Undisclosed positions must meet the "substantial authority" standard (roughly 40% likelihood), while disclosed positions (via Form 8275 or 8275-R) need only meet the lower "reasonable basis" standard (roughly 20%). The rationale is that disclosure gives the IRS notice to allocate examination resources to the position.
Wrong (A): The standard explicitly varies based on whether the position is disclosed; "more likely than not" applies only to tax shelter positions under Section 6694(a)(2)(C).
Wrong (C): This reverses the standards — disclosure earns a lower threshold, not a higher one.
Wrong (D): The "realistic possibility of success" standard was replaced by the current two-tier framework.$EXPL$
