  choices = $EXPL$["Both David and Ellen qualify for HOH because supporting any relative in a nursing home satisfies the residency requirement under the Code","Neither qualifies for HOH because the dependent must physically live in the taxpayer''s home for all dependents, with no exceptions for parents or other relatives","David qualifies because a dependent parent need not live with the taxpayer under Section 2(b)(1)(B), but Ellen does not qualify because her aunt must reside in Ellen''s home","Ellen qualifies but David does not, because the parent exception actually requires the parent to live with the taxpayer while other relatives may reside separately"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Section 2(b)(1)(B) creates a specific exception for dependent parents — the parent need not live with the taxpayer, so long as the taxpayer maintains the household where the parent lives (such as paying nursing home costs). No similar exception exists for aunts or other qualifying relatives. Ellen''s aunt must physically reside in Ellen''s home for more than half the year.
Wrong (A): The nursing home exception applies only to parents, not to all relatives.
Wrong (B): The parent exception explicitly overrides the general residency rule for HOH purposes.
