-- Q2392: Circular 230 [medium/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Oral advice is not governed by Circular 230 and falls outside the scope of the practitioner''s regulatory obligations","The practitioner must not consider the possibility the return will not be audited, and must base advice on reasonable factual and legal assumptions","Oral advice must be followed up with a formal written opinion within 30 days to comply with Circular 230 documentation requirements","The practitioner must disclose all oral advice to the IRS within the tax year in which the advice was provided to the client"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Circular 230 Section 10.37, the standards for written and oral advice are essentially the same. The practitioner must base advice on reasonable factual and legal assumptions, consider all relevant facts, and must not take into account the possibility that the return will not be audited or the issue will not be raised.
Wrong (A): Circular 230 Section 10.37 explicitly governs oral advice, not just written opinions.
Wrong (C): No 30-day follow-up requirement exists — oral advice does not require subsequent written confirmation.
Wrong (D): There is no requirement to disclose oral advice to the IRS.$EXPL$
