-- Q2396: Circular 230 [hard/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["No sanction because the error was caused by the tax software and not by the CPA''s independent judgment","Criminal prosecution for tax fraud based on the $15,000 understatement resulting from the incorrect code section","Automatic disbarment from practice before the IRS without any intermediate censure or suspension step","Sanctions for failure to exercise due diligence and competence in preparing and verifying the return"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Circular 230 Section 10.22, a practitioner must exercise due diligence in preparing and filing tax returns. Relying on outdated software without independently verifying the applicable tax code constitutes a failure of due diligence. This sanctionable conduct under Section 10.50 may result in censure, suspension, or monetary penalties.
Wrong (A): A CPA retains professional responsibility regardless of whether software caused the error.
Wrong (B): Reliance on outdated software does not rise to the level of willful fraud warranting criminal prosecution.
Wrong (C): Automatic disbarment is reserved for the most egregious misconduct; a due diligence failure typically results in lesser sanctions.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2396;

-- Q2398: Circular 230 [medium/L2]
