-- Q2415: Professional Ethics in Tax [medium/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Accept the $5,000 estimate without question and include it on the return as reported by the client","Require the client to sign a separate indemnification agreement for the estimated amount before including it on the return","Refuse to include any amount for business expenses on the return without original receipts documenting each expenditure","Make reasonable inquiries about the nature and basis of the estimate, and include it only if it appears reasonable under the circumstances"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under SSTS No. 4, a CPA may use client estimates when exact data is unavailable, provided the CPA exercises professional judgment about the estimate''s reasonableness. The CPA should inquire about the basis for the estimate and consider whether it is consistent with the client''s occupation and income level.
Wrong (A): Accepting estimates without inquiry fails to meet the standard of professional care required by SSTS No. 4.
Wrong (B): No indemnification agreement is required — the standard requires reasonable inquiry, not legal waivers.
Wrong (C): SSTS No. 4 permits reasonable estimates; categorical refusal of all estimates without receipts is not required.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2415;

-- Q2417: Professional Ethics in Tax [medium/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The strategy involves significant legal uncertainty and the client could face substantial penalties if the position is not sustained on its merits","The amount of tax savings is less than $1,000 and therefore falls below the threshold requiring written documentation","The client has been a long-time client and trusts the CPA''s oral recommendations based on their established professional relationship","Written advice is only necessary for listed transactions specifically identified by the IRS in published guidance"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
