Wrong (A): Partners cannot allocate losses arbitrarily — Section 704(b) requires substantial economic effect.
Wrong (B): Strict proportional allocation is not required; special allocations are permitted if they meet the economic effect test.
Wrong (C): Special allocations are not inherently fraudulent — they are a legitimate tax planning tool when properly structured.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2424;

